value was missed. A Ritz pair is accepted when its residual","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" · max(|λ|, s\/1000), s Gershgorin’s bound on the spectrum; the vectors","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, whose values are returned. The dense solver below 64","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, or when k is a third of them or more.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"10) for the basis.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position."}]},{"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smallest"},{"type":"text","text":" is in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0...vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", every weight is finite,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}]}],"style":"note"},{"name":"Throws","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" when a Lanczos run spends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":" products without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"converging, with the products spent and the largest Ritz residual on the tolerance’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scale. The dense solver thro